# Memory Bank: backend/src/controllers/material.controller.ts

## Purpose
This file contains the `MaterialController` class, which is responsible for handling HTTP requests related to project materials. It acts as an intermediary between the Express routes and the `materialService`.

## How it Works
- Each public method in the `MaterialController` class corresponds to a specific API endpoint action (e.g., creating, retrieving, updating, deleting materials).
- Methods parse request parameters (like `projectId`, `materialId`) and request bodies (`materialData`).
- They call corresponding methods in the `materialService` to perform the business logic and database interactions.
- They use a `handleServiceResponse` utility (assumed to exist) to standardize sending responses (success or error) back to the client.
- Error handling is implemented using try-catch blocks to manage exceptions and send appropriate HTTP status codes.
- **Crucially, request handlers now use `CustomRequest` (imported from `../middlewares/auth.middleware`) to ensure correct typing for `req.user` when accessed after authentication.**

## Key Methods
- `createMaterial(req: CustomRequest, res: Response)`:
  - Handles `POST /projects/:projectId/materials`.
  - Extracts `projectId` and `materialData` from the request.
  - Calls `materialService.createMaterial()`.
- `getMaterialsByProject(req: CustomRequest, res: Response)`:
  - Handles `GET /projects/:projectId/materials`.
  - Extracts `projectId`.
  - Calls `materialService.getMaterialsByProject()`.
- `getMaterialById(req: CustomRequest, res: Response)`:
  - Handles `GET /materials/:materialId`.
  - Extracts `materialId`.
  - Calls `materialService.getMaterialById()`.
- `updateMaterial(req: CustomRequest, res: Response)`:
  - Handles `PUT /materials/:materialId`.
  - Extracts `materialId` and `materialData`.
  - Calls `materialService.updateMaterial()`.
- `deleteMaterial(req: CustomRequest, res: Response)`:
  - Handles `DELETE /materials/:materialId`.
  - Extracts `materialId`.
  - Calls `materialService.deleteMaterial()`.

## Inputs
- `CustomRequest` objects (which include Express `Request` properties and an authenticated `user` object).
- `Response` objects from Express.
- Data from `req.params` and `req.body`.
- DTOs like `CreateMaterialDto`, `UpdateMaterialDto` (currently from `../bim/types/bim.types`).

## Outputs
- HTTP responses to clients via the `res` object, typically JSON.
- Logs errors to the console.

## Dependencies
- `express` (Request, Response types).
- `http-status-codes` (for standardized HTTP status codes).
- `../services/material.service` (for business logic).
- `../middlewares/auth.middleware` (for `CustomRequest` type).
- `../common/utils/httpHandlers` (for `handleServiceResponse`).
- `../bim/types/bim.types` (for DTOs).

## Recent Changes (2025-05-10)
- Updated all request handler methods (`createMaterial`, `getMaterialsByProject`, etc.) to use `CustomRequest` as the type for the `req` parameter instead of the generic Express `Request`. This aligns with the `isAuthenticated` middleware and resolves TypeScript errors related to `req.user`.
- Imported `CustomRequest` from `../middlewares/auth.middleware`.

## Flow Diagram (Conceptual for `createMaterial`)
```mermaid
graph TD
    RouteHandler[project.routes.ts router.post('/:projectId/materials', materialController.createMaterial)] --> MCCreate{materialController.createMaterial}
    MCCreate --> ParseRequest{Parse req.params.projectId, req.body}
    ParseRequest --> ValidateInput{Validate projectId}
    ValidateInput -- Valid --> CallService{materialService.createMaterial(projectId, materialData)}
    ValidateInput -- Invalid --> BadRequestResponse[400 Bad Request]
    CallService --> ServiceResponse{ServiceResponse (success/error)}
    ServiceResponse --> HandleResponseUtil{handleServiceResponse(serviceResponse, res)}
    HandleResponseUtil --> ClientResponse[HTTP Response to Client]
    MCCreate -- OnError --> ErrorHandler{Catch Block}
    ErrorHandler --> LogError{console.error}
    ErrorHandler --> InternalErrorResponse[500 Internal Server Error]
    InternalErrorResponse --> ClientResponse
